@startuml
left to right direction
skinparam backgroundColor #ffffff
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 15
skinparam defaultFontColor #111827
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam arrowColor #4b5563
skinparam rectangleBackgroundColor #f3f4f6
skinparam rectangleBorderColor #4b5563
skinparam usecaseBackgroundColor #ffffff
skinparam usecaseBorderColor #4b5563
skinparam actorBorderColor #4b5563
skinparam actorBackgroundColor #f3f4f6
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #e5e7eb
skinparam noteBorderColor #4b5563
skinparam nodesep 14
skinparam ranksep 30

title Market Desk | local shopper goals through J12
actor Shopper as shopper
actor "Consumer Council\nprice feed" as feed
actor "AI explanation service\n(optional; checked facts only)" as ai
rectangle "Local Market Desk - one user, H2 file" as App {
  usecase "Find and compare\naccepted products / offer text" as search
  usecase "Manage My list\n(quantity, retailer, checked state)" as list
  usecase "Review planned budget\nand category estimates" as budget
  usecase "Save / remove\nwishlist products" as wishlist
  usecase "Track one or all retailers\nfor an exact product" as track
  usecase "Manage target / drop alerts,\ntiming, read state and snooze" as alerts
  usecase "Manage interval reminders;\nclear, snooze or add to My list" as reminder
  usecase "Ask about one product from\nchecked catalogue facts" as ask
  usecase "Export a list or import\na separate validated copy" as transfer
  usecase "Download a read-only\noffline list snapshot" as offline
  usecase "Choose English, Chinese\nand contrast" as language
  usecase "View, export or delete\npersonal records" as privacy
  usecase "View a tracked product's\nobservation history and gaps" as history
  usecase "Load checked sample" as sample
  usecase "Refresh live prices" as refresh
}
shopper -- search
shopper -- list
shopper -- budget
shopper -- wishlist
shopper -- track
shopper -- alerts
shopper -- reminder
shopper -- ask
shopper -- transfer
shopper -- offline
shopper -- language
shopper -- privacy
shopper -- history
shopper -- sample
shopper -- refresh
refresh -- feed
ask -- ai
note right of App
  **Reading this view**
  Saving, tracking, and adding to My list
  are separate actions.

  History records changes after accepted
  LIVE imports. The sample is excluded.

  Alerts and reminders are in-app.
  A closed app collects and delivers nothing.

  Budgets describe a shopping plan,
  not purchases or actual spending.

  Ask uses the AI only to explain checked
  facts; search and fallback stay local.

  Joined lists are separate file copies,
  not live sync. The offline snapshot is static.

  Personal-data deletion keeps the accepted
  catalogue and its source metadata.

  The feed and AI are supporting actors.
  Only the shopper starts a refresh or asks.
end note
@enduml
